c(38, "§4.5 table (verbatim)", "data-caveat", "Rating / text contradictions (verbatim): a 5★ reporting a date-rendering bug ('the calendar is a day out… would be perfect if fixed'); a 5★ reporting the UI switching language unprompted — both inflate the mean; with zero 1★/2★ they support the conclusion that star ratings systematically understate friction: use theme counts, not the star average", "n/a", "mixed", table("## 4.5 Rating / text contradictions", 0), "none", "table", "generalisable", ["14201101389","14194139904"])
